+Batch54: rename a saved outfit through an explicit Rename action on its card. Reuse the existing outfit-name form, 16-character name cleaning and replaceOutfit helper. A rename updates only the matching saved name; use the saved outfit's own equipped value, never the currently worn look. Preserve ID, list order, other looks, current wearing, preview pose/mirror/pause and clock. A blank rename keeps the existing name and a no-op produces no save. If the target disappears while editing, close without recreating it or writing stale state. Read the latest target on submit. Duplicate names retain the existing allowed policy. Keep new-outfit saving and removal confirmation available and distinct.
+
+Use native name input, Save name, Not now and Escape cancellation; focus/select the existing name when opening and return keyboard focus to the card's Rename control after saving or canceling. One editor at a time; switching target discards only unsaved text. No new timers, schema, dependency, background writes or external service. Keep Rename and Remove as stacked full-width card actions at compact widths and verify name wrapping, focus, native keyboard, persisted-only-name changes and the paused preview at 100/200-percent text in portrait and landscape. Add meaningful controlled Wardrobe unit cases and an offline native regression before implementation. Keep every diagnostic and exact candidate binding; use the existing one-heavy-job resource guard.
+
+Initial controlled red:10missing-control failures and1existing new-save case passes; native initial case rejects missing Rename. The first isolated candidate passes11unit/native cases but lacks native paint visibility checks. Root short-phone still inspection exposes clipped returned focus. A new native hit-test assertion reproduces that at320/100. Nearest scrolling fixes that view but leaves5of11 enlarged/landscape cases clipped; disabling finite CSS transitions for static PNGs changes only capture settling, and the same5failures remain. Centered return passes11cases and native Tab/Space cancellation, but a new name-paint check reproduces a partly hidden saved label at844/200. The final candidate scrolls the complete action stack to the end of the scrollport, with6px scroll margin, then focuses Rename without a second scroll. This retains the saved name above the actions and passes all11native cases with actual elementFromPoint checks for both focus and name, including native cancellation.
+
+Retain initial, nearest, centered and final candidate source bytes and each fixture revision. Native final-candidate fixtures now seed all16wearables as earned so card art matches saved looks; this is fixture data only. CSS transitions are disabled only for static screenshots, not for native motion sampling. A newly saved look returns focus to its own Rename action. There are no production edits until candidate source, behavior and stills are reviewed. All original accepted greeting bytes are preserved at b5987ae.
+
+Applied the reviewed action-stack candidate, then the114focused checks pass. Final-candidate still inspection also reveals that the pixel100px name-field basis squeezes selected Weekend to its trailing letters at1280/200. A native readable-width assertion reproduces it before changing styles. Set the field basis to10rem, retaining min-width0/max-width100percent and wrapping buttons. This scales the input with text and lets it use its own row when needed. Preserve the21action-stack stills as reviewed diagnostics, with their original CSS hash/path. Final production checks and visual review cover the corrected field.
+
